AB  - Compound heatwaves increasingly trigger cascading failures that propagate through interconnected physical and human systems, yet the fragmentation of disciplinary knowledge hinders comprehensive mapping of these systemic risk topologies. This study introduces the Heatwave Discovery Agent (HeDA), an autonomous scientific synthesis framework designed to bridge disciplinary gaps by constructing a knowledge graph from 8365 academic publications. The system structures 34,933 entities and 42,890 directed relationships from a temporally partitioned corpus (≤2024, n = 5,739). On a temporally held-out multi-hop reasoning benchmark (2025–2026, n = 3,892), knowledge-graph augmentation yields a consistent accuracy improvement of 8.1% to 9.8% over four standalone foundation-model baselines (McNemar exact test, p<10−19). Topological analysis identifies a bio-ecological mediation effect in which biological systems function as the primary structural mediators of thermal stress, transforming physical meteorological hazards into systemic socioeconomic losses. We further identify latent functional couplings between theoretically distinct sectors, such as the heat-induced synchronization of power grid failures and emergency medical capacity saturation. These findings provide a structural basis for shifting adaptation strategies from static sectoral defense to dynamic cross-system resilience.
ER  - 

