AB  - The PRISMA 2020-compliant systematic literature review framework is indispensable for evidence synthesis in engineering research; however, it remains resource-intensive, time-consuming, and susceptible to human inconsistency. This paper presents an AI-assisted systematic review pipeline employing a large language model (claude-opus-4-5, Anthropic) comprising ten sequential modules automating the PRISMA 2020-compliant workflow, including title screening, abstract screening, full-text eligibility, data extraction, bibliometric analysis, thematic synthesis, and gap identification, culminating in automatic generation of a structured manuscript template. Five algorithms are formally documented in pseudocode; a single configuration file controls the workflow, enabling the application to new domains without code modification. Applied to digital twins for bridge predictive maintenance and lifecycle management, a Scopus search retrieved 90 records (2020–2026), from which 20 high-quality articles were identified, all receiving HIGH confidence ratings, revealing five thematic clusters and six critical gaps. The pipeline is provided as open supplementary code.
